# Modelfile for qcgemma4-st — the AI quality-check model.
#
# Gemma 4 E4B IT fine-tuned on scripts/qc_dataset_sharegpt.jsonl (14,928
# examples over the 16 issue codes below, generated by
# scripts/create_qc_dataset.py).
#
# YOU PROBABLY DO NOT NEED THIS FILE. Unlike the translation fine-tunes, the QC
# model is published on the Ollama hub:
#
#   ollama pull 0xra/bethesda-qc
#   ollama cp   0xra/bethesda-qc qcgemma4-st
#
# This Modelfile is for rebuilding it from a local GGUF — your own export, or a
# stock Gemma 4 E4B IT, since the SYSTEM prompt below is what drives the
# structured output and an un-tuned instruct model gives usable (if noisier)
# verdicts.
#
# IMPORTANT — parameter precedence:
#   gui/ai_qc_worker.py calls /api/generate with its own `system` and with
#   temperature 0.0 and num_predict 1024, so those three are overridden on every
#   API call. It sends nothing else — num_ctx and the stop tokens below are what
#   apply at runtime. (The SYSTEM here is kept identical to _SYSTEM_PROMPT in
#   that module so `ollama run qcgemma4-st` behaves the same as the app.)
#
# To build from this file:
#   1. Point the FROM line at a Gemma 4 E4B IT GGUF on your machine.
#   2. ollama create qcgemma4-st -f Modelfile.qc
#   3. Settings → Quality → "AI QC model" (default: qcgemma4-st), and tick
#      "AI quality check". The name is free-form: whatever you build here must
#      match what that field says.
#
# Input format, matching the training data:
#   Check this Ukrainian translation:
#
#   Source (English):
#   {source}
#
#   Translation (Ukrainian):
#   {translation}

FROM /path/to/gemma-4-e4b-it.Q4_K_M.gguf

# ── Chat template (Gemma format) ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# Gemma marks turns with <start_of_turn>/<end_of_turn>; there is no <|turn>
# variant in this family, and a template that invents one leaves the model with
# no reachable stop token, so every check runs to the num_predict cap.
TEMPLATE "{{ if .System }}<start_of_turn>system
{{ .System }}<end_of_turn>
{{ end }}{{ if .Prompt }}<start_of_turn>user
{{ .Prompt }}<end_of_turn>
{{ end }}<start_of_turn>model
{{ .Response }}<end_of_turn>"

SYSTEM "You are a quality checker for Bethesda Starfield Ukrainian game localization. Given a source string and its Ukrainian translation, detect quality issues.

Issue codes to detect:
  MISSING_TAG        — game format tag present in source but absent in translation
  EXTRA_TAG          — tag in translation not present in source
  SOURCE_LANGUAGE_LEAK — Russian characters (ы/э/ё/ъ) or Russian words in Ukrainian output
  ENGLISH_LEAK       — untranslated English words remaining in Ukrainian output
  UNTRANSLATED       — translation is identical to the source
  EMPTY_TRANSLATION  — translation is empty or whitespace-only
  SUSPICIOUSLY_SHORT — translation is <20% the length of the source
  SUSPICIOUSLY_LONG  — translation is >500% the length of the source
  AI_ARTIFACT        — AI commentary prefix (Note:, Translation:, Переклад:, etc.)
  REPETITIVE_CONTENT — same phrase repeated 3+ times (hallucination)
  MISSING_NEWLINES   — source has \\n but translation has none
  NEWLINE_COUNT_MISMATCH — newline count differs between source and translation
  MISSING_NUMBER     — standalone number in source absent from translation
  LOW_UKRAINIAN_COVERAGE — too few recognized Ukrainian words (<25%)
  CASE_MISMATCH      — source starts uppercase, translation starts lowercase
  TRANSLATION_TRUNCATED — translation is a cut-off prefix of the source

Output for clean translation:
VERDICT: GOOD

Output for problematic translation:
VERDICT: ISSUES_FOUND
CODES: CODE1, CODE2
SEVERITY: error|warning|info
DETAILS:
- [CODE] description
ACTION: AUTOFIX|RETRANSLATE"

# ── Generation parameters ────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Deterministic: a QC verdict must not vary between runs on the same pair.
# (The app sends 0.0 as well.)
PARAMETER temperature 0.0

# Context window: source + translation + the ~400-token system prompt. Not sent
# by the app, so this is the value in force.
PARAMETER num_ctx 8192

# Output budget. The model reasons before emitting the VERDICT block, and a
# truncated verdict parses as no issues found — which is exactly the failure a
# quality checker must not have. The app sends 1024 as well.
PARAMETER num_predict 1024

# ── Stop tokens ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
PARAMETER stop <end_of_turn>
PARAMETER stop <start_of_turn>
